# NestJS Project Guidelines

## Project guideline

1. use yarn
2. avoid using configuration service for loading env, use `process.env` instead

## Project Structure

1. Follow the modular architecture:
```
src/
├── app.module.ts          # Root module
├── main.ts               # Application entry point
├── modules/              # Feature modules
│   └── [feature]/
│       ├── dto/         # Data Transfer Objects
│       ├── entities/    # Database entities
│       ├── interfaces/  # TypeScript interfaces
│       ├── [feature].controller.ts
│       ├── [feature].service.ts
│       ├── [feature].module.ts
│       └── [feature].repository.ts
├── common/              # Shared resources
│   ├── decorators/
│   ├── filters/
│   ├── guards/
│   ├── interceptors/
│   └── pipes/
└── config/             # Configuration files
    └── environment.ts
```

## Naming Conventions

1. Files:
   - Use kebab-case for filenames
   - Include the type in the filename (e.g., `user.controller.ts`)
   - Test files should end with `.spec.ts`
   - Always insert a new line at the of the file

2. Classes:
   - Use PascalCase
   - Append type to class name (e.g., `UserController`, `UserService`)
   ```typescript
   // Good
   export class UserController {}
   
   // Bad
   export class userController {}
   ```

3. Methods and Properties:
   - Use camelCase
   - HTTP methods should be descriptive
   ```typescript
   // Good
   async findUserById() {}
   async createNewUser() {}
   
   // Bad
   async getUser() {}
   async post() {}
   ```

## Decorator Usage

1. Controller Decorators:
   ```typescript
   @Controller('users')
   @ApiBearerAuth('JWT')
   export class UserController {
     @Get(':id')
     @UseGuards(AuthGuard)
     async findOne(@Param('id') id: string) {}
   }
   ```

2. Service Decorators:
   ```typescript
   @Injectable()
   export class UserService {
     constructor(
       @InjectRepository(User)
       private readonly userRepository: Repository<User>,
     ) {}
   }
   ```

## DTOs and Validation

1. Always use DTOs for request/response data:
   ```typescript
   export class CreateUserDto {
     @IsString()
     @IsNotEmpty()
     readonly name: string;

     @IsEmail()
     readonly email: string;

     @IsString()
     @MinLength(8)
     readonly password: string;
   }
   ```

2. Implement class-validator decorators for validation

3. always use swagger decorator in the DTOs

## Exception Handling

1. Use built-in HTTP exceptions:
   ```typescript
   // Good
   throw new NotFoundException('User not found');
   
   // Bad
   throw new Error('User not found');
   ```

2. Create custom exception filters when needed:
   ```typescript
   @Catch(HttpException)
   export class HttpExceptionFilter implements ExceptionFilter {
     catch(exception: HttpException, host: ArgumentsHost) {
       // Implementation
     }
   }
   ```

## Dependency Injection

1. Constructor-based injection:
   ```typescript
   // Good
   constructor(private readonly userService: UserService) {}
   
   // Bad
   @Inject(UserService)
   private readonly userService: UserService;
   ```

## Testing

1. Unit Tests:
   - Test files should be adjacent to the file they test
   - Use descriptive test names
   ```typescript
   describe('UserService', () => {
     it('should create a new user with valid data', () => {
       // Test implementation
     });
   });
   ```

2. E2E Tests:
   - Place in separate `test` directory
   - Use `supertest` for HTTP requests

## Environment Configuration

1. Use ConfigService for environment variables:
   ```typescript
   constructor(private configService: ConfigService) {
     const dbHost = this.configService.get<string>('DATABASE_HOST');
   }
   ```

2. Validate environment variables using Joi

## API Documentation

1. Use Swagger decorators for API documentation:
   ```typescript
   @ApiTags('users')
   @ApiResponse({ status: 201, description: 'User created successfully' })
   @Post()
   async create(@Body() createUserDto: CreateUserDto) {}
   ```
1. Use Swagger decoratir for DTOs

## Performance Best Practices

1. Use caching when appropriate:
   ```typescript
   @CacheKey('users')
   @CacheTTL(30)
   async findAll() {}
   ```

2. Implement pagination for list endpoints:
   ```typescript
   @Get()
   async findAll(
     @Query('page') page: number = 1,
     @Query('limit') limit: number = 10,
   ) {}
   ```

